# Mirror registry cluster resources (generated by oc-mirror v2)

**Do not edit this template manually.** After running `oc mirror` with `--v2`, apply the
YAML files from:

```
${OC_MIRROR_WORKDIR}/cluster-resources/
```

oc-mirror v2 generates (per [Red Hat documentation](https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.22/html/disconnected_environments/about-installing-oc-mirror-v2)):

| Resource | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `ImageDigestMirrorSet` (IDMS) | Maps release/operator images by digest |
| `ImageTagMirrorSet` (ITMS) | Maps images by tag |
| `CatalogSource` | Mirrored `redhat-operator-index` for OperatorHub |

> **OpenShift 4.22:** `ImageContentSourcePolicy` (ICSP) is deprecated for new installs.
> Use IDMS/ITMS from oc-mirror v2 output instead.

## Apply after cluster install

```bash
oc apply -f "${OC_MIRROR_WORKDIR}/cluster-resources/"
```

## Apply before agent ISO generation (disconnected install)

Per the [Agent-based Installer disconnected mirroring guide](https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.22/html/installing_an_on-premise_cluster_with_the_agent-based_installer/understanding-disconnected-installation-mirroring):

1. Merge `additionalTrustBundle` (mirror registry CA) into `install-config.yaml`
2. Embed mirror mapping in `install-config.yaml` or mount `registries.conf` (TOML v2) into the agent ISO
3. Use the **cluster pull secret** in `install-config.yaml` — not the mirror-registry credentials file

Scripts `03-generate-install-config.sh` and `04-mirror-ocp-images.sh` automate these steps
where possible.
